A few months ago I ascended my first character on NAO, a Valkyrie, and
decided that it'd be easy to do it again with another character. Not
wanting to overdo it, I picked a Barbarian, which I felt would
compliment the playing style I'd developed using the Valk. Overall,
things went well, although both good and bad luck marred the game, and
my own stupidity probably could've ruined things.

The mines were fraught with danger, as usual. A nymph robbed me blind
and led me on a merry chase for what seemed like ages before I could
get my weapon, armor, and lamp back. A troll/vampire tagteam near
Mines' End would've been the end of me if not for a wand of teleport
I'd found just moments earlier. I came back after sacrificing for
Cleaver and Trollbane and finished him off. Dwarves in the minds were
nice enough to lend me their equipment, which kept my AC around -10
until the castle. The rest of the mines and Sokoban went easily enough
(found a +4 ring of Protection in the former and a BoH in the latter).
I found a couple more altars on the way down to Medusa's and sacrificed
hoping for Frost brand, but I only got Mjollnir for my efforts. A few
bones on the way down provided me with some nice things, like a cloak
of MR.

Now for a story. My first character on NAO, another Valk, met an early
end at the hands of the Titan on Medusa's Level. She fell down a hole
while Wraith-baiting, took a few steps to get her bearings, and got hit
by three doses of Summon Nasties before she even realized what level
she was on. So when my Barbarian took a page out my Valk's book and
fell through a hole into a familiar-looking room, I quickly found the
stairs and burned Elbereth on them. Within the next few turns I was
badly mobbed, but E kept most of the monsters at bay. I tried
desperately to land a few hits on the Titan, but couldn't reach him. In
the end I had to resort to digging downward and coming back later,
after I'd wished up some better equipment at the Castle.

Castle was uneventful. I wished up or found all the equipment I needed
and enchanted it up. I didn't do a very good job at it. Somehow, I
managed to forget that +4 was the cap on enchanting, so I lost    a
pair of speed boots, costing a wish. I did, however, manage to get +7
SDSM before I realized it couldn't be done. :) So I ended up wasting
two wishes: one on another pair of boots, another by pressing an arrow
key while writing up a wish (bad idea).

I stopped playing for about two months here, then started again at the
Quest, where I found a magic marker and a magic lamp, which made much
better prizes than the Heart of Ahriman. From there I went into
Gehennom, where nothing much happened until I reached Orcus-Town.
There, I broke one of the cardinal rules of Nethack and read an un-IDed
scroll, which happened to evaporate my Cloak of Magic Resistance. I
made plans to polymorph into a Lich to survive Rodney later before I
realized I still had a magic lamp left. Before I could use it, however,
I found another, so I got to both keep my cloak of MR and my light
source. Thanks, RNG!

Finding the VS was almost no trouble at all for a change, and Yeenoghu
was nice enough to steal the AoY for me at Moloch's Sanctum. I marched
all the way back to DL1 without encountering Rodney even once. I used
my remaining magic lamp on a wand of death. The elemental planes went
well thanks to ?oGD, although the Plane of Air turned out to be
painful. I found a Helm of Opposite Alignment on the Plane of Water,
but decided that I wasn't going to use it. That could've been a big
mistake.

Astral Plane was terrible. The moment I opened the right-hand door I
got paralyzed and badly withered by Famine. Oops, forgot to put on
=oFR. I plowed through, but the altar wasn't mine so I went back.
Famine revived a ridiculous number of times, but /oD took care of him
for the most part. Next, the left door. I charge in, a bit
overconfident. Death lowers my max hitpoints a bit, but it doesn't
matter much.

Then "Ken the Spelunker" takes off my head with a +8 Vorpal Blade in
one hit. I'd heard about this happening, but was sure that it'd never
happen to me. Luckily I'd put on the Amulet of Lifesaving I'd found at
Vlad's. I carefully stoned Ken with a cockatrice corpse I'd saved and
relieved him of the sword. Again, wrong altar. I went back, opened the
center door, and dashed through before I could get hit by any other
surprises.

I learned three things from this game:
1. Don't forget about the caps on enchanting.
2. Never, ever read un-IDed scrolls, especially if they're price IDed
at 100. Dumb.
3. Watch out for player-monsters on the planes; they might behead you.

Next run, I'll try an Archaelogist. It seemed to work for Ken the
Spelunker, anyway.


